FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] src/analyzer.rs:296 — `RepeatUntil` analyzes the condition before walking the body, so a condition reading a name the body binds (`repeat / set t to 1 / until t is 1`) is reported `Unknown variable 't'` (src/analyzer.rs:426) even though the write lands in program scope (src/analyzer.rs:100) and both VMs would succeed at runtime, since the body runs first — valid post-test programs are falsely rejected — fix: walk the body first, then analyze the condition.
2. [MAJOR] src/formatter.rs:134 — `closing_lines` collects only `Else`/`Catch`/`Finally`/`End` and omits `Until`, but `Statement::RepeatUntil` (src/formatter.rs:387) formats its body via `format_block`/`emit_block_tail`, which consumes the next closing as its own — tail comments of a repeat-until body are misattached and the outer block's `End` is consumed (`next_closing`/`last_line` corrupted), so formatting a repeat-until inside any `... end` block corrupts what follows — fix: include `Until` in `closing_lines`.
3. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/codegen.rs:401 — the post-test condition and its backward `JUMP_IF_FALSE` are emitted with `line` = the `repeat` statement's line, and the tree-walker evaluates the condition under the outer statement span (src/interpreter.rs:1285), so a failing condition (e.g. `xs[99]` on the `until` line) names the `repeat` line instead of the `until` line where it was written — no test pins a condition span (the suite pins only the body span at tests/repeat_until_test.rs:337) — fix: thread the `until` token's line/span into the compiled condition and the evaluated condition.
4. [MAJOR] src/interpreter.rs:1282 — a `skip` in a post-test loop `continue`s without reading the condition, so an every-turn-skipped loop never exits on its own; which limit stops it (per-loop `Maximum ... 'repeat'` vs step-budget) and whether both engines agree is untested — the phase's own FINDINGS.md §4 admits step-budget termination without a test — fix: add `edge_every_turn_skipped_is_stopped_by_the_iteration_cap_on_both_vms` asserting the `Maximum of N iterations ... 'repeat' loop` error on both engines under a cap.
5. [MINOR] src/parser.rs:989 — `opens_post_test_loop` is true only on an immediate `Newline`, so the one-line form `repeat set n to n + 1 until n is 3` is misrouted to the counted path and refused, and a bare `repeat` at EOF (`None != Newline`) takes the counted path with a confusing expression error instead of a missing-`until` diagnostic — fix: accept same-line `until` or emit a dedicated diagnostic, and add a test for each.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
